<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grover Cleveland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837–1908</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grover Cleveland was the 22nd and 24th president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, serving from 1885 to 1889 and from 1893 to 1897. A Democrat who opposed high tariffs and defended the gold standard, he withdrew the treaty to annex <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> in 1893 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blount-report">Blount Report</a> found American complicity in the queen's overthrow. His second term was dominated by the economic depression that followed the Panic of 1893.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grover-cleveland.jpg" alt="Grover Cleveland" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Napoleon Sarony · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:StephenGroverCleveland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
